<title>AUSTRIA: Italy's Ciampi sees agreement on stability pact.</title>
<headline>Italy's Ciampi sees agreement on stability pact.</headline>
<dateline>VIENNA 1996-12-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Italian Treasury Minister Carlo Azeglio Ciampi said on Wednesday he expected European Union (EU) finance ministers to agree on a proposed budget stability pact for economic and monetary union (EMU) at a meeting in Dublin next week.</p>
<p>&quot;I am convinced it will come to an agreement, literally the evening before the meeting in Dublin,&quot; Ciampi told journalists in Vienna after meeting his Austrian counterpart Viktor Klima.</p>
<p>EU finance ministers failed to agree on a stability pact aimed at ensuring lasting compliance with EMU entry criteria at a meeting this week but are scheduled to meet again in Dublin on the eve of a EU summit planned for December 13-14. -- Knut Engelmann, Vienna newsroom +431 53112 274</p>
